exports[`K5 snapshots post kit, a reel with every capability on and the repair turn's refusals 1`] = `
"WHAT YOU CAN USE — the capability library for this post, generated from the app's own list. One line per thing this app can do with the athlete's own media: what it does, what it needs, its settings, what it costs, how likely it is to show someone who is not her ("likeness risk"), when to use it and when not to, and what was measured. Plan only with these lines; nothing else is possible here. A line's needs are real: use it only when the candidate or the post has what it needs. A $0 line that carries the moment beats anything fancier.
THIS POST: reel, 9:16, up to 30 s, with sound. Moment: <external_content>home opener</external_content>, 2026-10-15, 3 days from today. Names a partner: no. Candidates: 2 photos, 2 clips, fastest clip 60 fps.
SHOTS — each picture or clip in the post is one of these
- clip.camera | does: A window of a clip she filmed, trimmed to the beat it covers. | needs: A CLIP line from her camera whose beats cover the moment. | cost: $0 (a trim of her own footage — nothing is generated) | likeness risk: none | use when: Any moment her camera covers. The first choice for a shot of her doing the thing. | don't use when: Holds none of an ad's hero opening, product or sign-off — the beats are what she filmed. | measured: On own-footage recaps it fills every slot it can: 10 of 10 on one plan, 26 of 26 cast slots over two briefs.
- clip.her_instagram | does: A window of a reel she posted, synced from her Instagram, trimmed to a beat. | needs: A CLIP line marked her instagram. | cost: $0 (a trim of her own posted footage) | likeness risk: none | use when: After her camera: it is her footage, but cut for a feed, often with text on it. | don't use when: Absent for most athletes today — plan as if it may not exist. | NOT measured: Unmeasured: the test athlete holds no stored Instagram video, so the live N is 0.
- image.held | does: One of her photos held on screen, dead still. | needs: A photo line; on an own-footage brief, a photo from her camera or one she picked. | cost: $0 (her photo, held — nothing is generated) | likeness risk: none | use when: A moment her clips do not cover, told by a photo of it. Prefer a pushed-in "image" over an "i2v" when the moment is a look, a pose or a place rather than an action. | don't use when: On an own-footage brief a made-here photo is swapped or left out. A screenshot, mockup or colour block is never cast unless she picked it. | measured: Renders in about half a second for a 4 s hold. Made-here and meta images are refused by the gates, not by taste.
PHOTO MOVES — on a photo in a reel or story, choose one
- image.motion.dolly | does: A slow centred push-in on a held photo — the frame ends 8% larger than it starts. | needs: An image item. | cost: $0 (an ffmpeg move on her photo) | likeness risk: none | use when: The fallback: a held photo with nothing in particular to arrive at, that should read as alive rather than as a slide. One thing to land on wants zoom; a wide frame wants sweep; a peak on a beat wants punch — dolly where none fits. | don't use when: Not a shot of her moving — that is an i2v, and it is not one. On a photo with a clear subject it wastes the arrival a zoom would make. | measured: The push-in A1b holds an own-footage i2v as; the renderer's quietest move.
- image.motion.zoom | does: The frame closes in on a point of the photo. | needs: An image item; a focus point, or the upper-middle framing prior. | cost: $0 (an ffmpeg move on her photo) | likeness risk: none | use when: A photo with one thing to arrive at — her face, a medal, the product. | don't use when: With no point and a busy frame it lands on the upper middle, whatever is there — a saliency point found her 0 of 8, so the prior is not a person finder. | measured: Untapped, it heads for the upper middle — within ~0.1 of her face in 8 of 8 portraits; give a focus point when the thing to arrive at sits elsewhere.
- image.motion.sweep | does: A move across the photo's long axis at a fixed size, toward the point's side. | needs: An image item; a focus point, or it crosses from the left. | cost: $0 (an ffmpeg move on her photo) | likeness risk: none | use when: A wide photo — a pitch, a line-up, a place — where the eye should travel. | don't use when: On a tight portrait it has nowhere to go. | measured: Same framing prior as zoom; the Board calls it Pan.
- image.motion.punch | does: A fast close-in to a point, then held — a snap on the peak. | needs: An image item; a focus point, or the framing prior. | cost: $0 (an ffmpeg move on her photo) | likeness risk: none | use when: A hype edit's peak — the goal, the result — set on a beat. | don't use when: In a slow, reflective edit it reads as a jolt. | measured: Same framing prior as zoom; lands on a beat when the plan is on the beat.
CLIP MOVES — on a clip, only when that clip has what the line needs
- clip.slow_mo | does: Plays one moment of a clip at half or quarter speed, using the real frames. | needs: A clip filmed at 59 fps or more; a moment of 1.5 s or less. | settings: factor (one of 2, 4); atSec (a number from 0 to 12) | cost: $0 (a retime of her own clip — nothing is generated) | likeness risk: none | use when: One peak: a finish, a landing, a celebration. | don't use when: The clip's own sound drops out for that moment while the music carries on. In a calm, talking clip it reads as a glitch. | NOT measured: Not yet: the retime probe lands with its own PR.
CARDS — at most one opener, and only when it makes the post clearly better
- card.title | does: A 2-second opening card with the hook, over the first shot dimmed. | needs: A hook of 40 characters or fewer. | settings: text (text, 40 characters or fewer) | cost: $0 (rendered here — nothing is generated) | likeness risk: none | use when: The hook reads better as words than as a picture. | don't use when: The first shot already says it — the card only delays her. | NOT measured: Not yet: render time and text fit land with its own PR.
- card.countdown | does: An opening "N days to [moment]" card; the number is worked out when the preview is made. | needs: A dated moment still ahead. | cost: $0 (rendered here — nothing is generated) | likeness risk: none | use when: A build-up post before a dated moment. | don't use when: A recap, or a post not tied to a date. | NOT measured: Not yet: the day count and re-render checks land with its own PR.
SOUND — one choice
- music.mood | does: The best licensed track for a mood, under the whole post. | needs: A mood from the list; a post that names a partner only gets tracks cleared for brand work. | settings: mood (one of hype, warm, reflective, bright, driving, dark, playful, uplifting, none) | cost: $0 (licensed, already in the bucket) | likeness risk: none | use when: A reel or story: the mood the moment carries. none when the post should be quiet. | don't use when: A mood with no track cleared for this post plays no music; the preview says so. | NOT measured: As a kit choice: the track is the catalogue's best for the mood; nobody has listened to the picks yet.
LOOKS — one look for the whole post
- look.preset | does: One colour look on every photo and clip of the post; natural changes nothing. | needs: A look name from the list. | settings: name (one of natural, warm, cool, vivid, muted, mono) | cost: $0 (one colour filter — nothing is generated) | likeness risk: none | use when: Every post. Prefer natural unless the brief or the pictures clearly call for another. | don't use when: A strong look on a picture that is already filtered stacks on top of it. | NOT measured: Each name is one fixed filter, the same on clips and photos; no cast check on clips yet.
FINISHING
- image.cutout | does: Lifts her cleanly off the background of one photo. | needs: A photo where she stands clear of other people. | cost: $0 (separated here — nothing is generated) | likeness risk: none | use when: As the first half of a new background or an ad card, never on its own. | don't use when: Fine hair and fingers can lose detail at the edge. Someone touching her in the frame makes the cut-out fail. | NOT measured: Not yet: the cut-out quality fixtures land with its own PR.
- image.background_place | does: Puts her, cut out, on a new background: a colour, a gradient, a scene with no people, or the partner's brand colour. | needs: A photo she can be cut out of cleanly; brand colour only on a post that names a partner. | settings: source (one of colour, gradient, scene, brand_colour); sceneTags (text, 80 characters or fewer) | cost: $0 (composed here — nothing is generated) | likeness risk: none | use when: The original background is cluttered or off-brand, or the photo is for an ad. | don't use when: The place is the story — her home ground, the finish line. Light and shadow come from the original photo, so a detailed scene can look pasted on; prefer a colour or gradient for close portraits. A scene never names a real place, and the caption must not say she was there. | NOT measured: Not yet: the placed-or-pasted check on each background lands with its own PR.
AUTOMATIC — the app does these on its own; do not ask for them
- caption: The post's hook laid over the opening of a reel or story, inside the safe zones. Needs: A hook of 80 characters or fewer with nothing in it the post must avoid.
- clip.stabilise: Steadies a clip that measures shaky, trimming about 5–8% off the edges. Needs: A kept clip that measures shaky; not a shot whose movement is shaky on purpose.
- caption.auto: Her spoken words as captions, timed to her voice, on any kept clip where she speaks. Needs: A kept clip with speech.
PAID — SHE DECIDES (never in the preview; only ever a button she taps)
(none offered here yet)
NOT AVAILABLE HERE YET — do not plan, offer or promise: image.recolour, image.garment, image.add_product, image.background_clean, image.ad_ai, image.apply_design, image.object.*, image.background_swap, image.relight, image.camera_angle, clip.reframe, card.stat, image.upscale, clip.upscale
IF A STEP IS REFUSED you get back its code and what to do instead:
  music.mood / no_track_for_mood: "No track carries that mood for this post. Choose another mood, or none."
  clip.slow_mo / fps_too_low: "This clip was filmed below 59 fps. Keep it at normal speed, or use image.motion.punch on a photo of the peak."
  clip.slow_mo / window_too_long: "Slow motion holds 1.5 s or less. Choose a shorter moment, or keep the clip at normal speed."
  image.cutout / cutout_not_clean: "She can't be cut out cleanly from this photo. Keep its own background, or pick a photo where she stands clear."
  image.background_place / cutout_not_clean: "She can't be cut out cleanly from this photo. Keep its own background, or pick a photo where she stands clear."
  image.background_place / brand_colour_without_partner: "Brand colour needs a post that names a partner. Use colour or gradient instead."
  card.title / text_too_long: "The card holds 40 characters or fewer. Shorten the line, or leave the card out."
  card.countdown / no_moment_ahead: "This post has no dated moment ahead. Leave the card out, or use card.title instead."
Fix the plan once using these; anything still refused is left out."
`;

exports[`K5 snapshots the Board's block 1`] = `
"WHAT YOU CAN PLAN — the capability library. One line per thing this app can make: what it does, what it needs, what it costs, how likely it is to draw someone who is not her ("likeness risk"), and what was measured. Plan against these lines, and name the one each choice came from in its "reason". A line's cost and risk are real: a $0 line that carries the moment beats a paid one that carries it no better.
- clip.camera → an item with "kind": "clip" on a CLIP line "from: her camera" | does: A window of a clip she filmed, trimmed to the beat it covers. | needs: A CLIP line from her camera whose beats cover the moment. | cost: $0 (a trim of her own footage — nothing is generated) | likeness risk: none | works: Any moment her camera covers. The first choice for a shot of her doing the thing. | fails: Holds none of an ad's hero opening, product or sign-off — the beats are what she filmed. | measured: On own-footage recaps it fills every slot it can: 10 of 10 on one plan, 26 of 26 cast slots over two briefs.
- clip.her_instagram → an item with "kind": "clip" on a CLIP line "from: her instagram" | does: A window of a reel she posted, synced from her Instagram, trimmed to a beat. | needs: A CLIP line marked her instagram. | cost: $0 (a trim of her own posted footage) | likeness risk: none | works: After her camera: it is her footage, but cut for a feed, often with text on it. | fails: Absent for most athletes today — plan as if it may not exist. | NOT measured: Unmeasured: the test athlete holds no stored Instagram video, so the live N is 0.
- clip.made_here → an item with "kind": "clip" on a CLIP line "from: made here" | does: A window of a clip made in the Studio earlier. | needs: A CLIP line marked made here. | cost: $0 (already made — reusing it spends nothing) | likeness risk: high | works: Last among clips: only where neither her camera nor her Instagram covers the moment. | fails: It was generated, so it can show someone who is not her. On a brief asking for her own footage it is never used unless she picked it (S1c) — it is left out. | measured: Cast on the ad brief when no camera beat fit (2 of 2 cells); a made-here clip may not show her at all.
- image.held → an item with "kind": "image" | does: One of her photos held on screen, dead still. | needs: A photo line; on an own-footage brief, a photo from her camera or one she picked. | cost: $0 (her photo, held — nothing is generated) | likeness risk: none | works: A moment her clips do not cover, told by a photo of it. Prefer a pushed-in "image" over an "i2v" when the moment is a look, a pose or a place rather than an action. | fails: On an own-footage brief a made-here photo is swapped or left out (S1b). A screenshot, mockup or colour block is never cast unless she picked it (A2). | measured: Renders in about half a second for a 4 s hold. Made-here and meta images are refused by the gates, not by taste.
- i2v → an item with "kind": "i2v" | does: One of her photos brought to life as a short generated shot of her moving. | needs: A photo she is in — her camera, synced, or one she picked; a made-here still only when identity-bound. | cost: $0.80 per 4 s shot, $1.60 with sound | likeness risk: high | works: She asked for her in motion and no clip of her camera covers that moment. | fails: Can draw someone who is not her. On an own-footage brief it never runs — A1b holds the photo pushed in. Complex action (three defenders, a top-corner finish) is where it invents. | measured: A model draws her: a generated still with no person reference was cast as her once. On an own-footage brief it is held pushed-in instead ($0).
- broll → an item with "kind": "broll" | does: A generated shot made from words alone — a place, an object, an atmosphere. Never her. | needs: Nothing from her library: a direction. | cost: $0.37 per 4 s shot | likeness risk: low | works: A gap no footage of hers covers and no person is needed for — the stadium, the gear, the city. | fails: An opener on a recap is not a gap: it stands in front of her own footage. Anything that needs her in it. | measured: Refuses real people by policy, so it cannot be her. On own-footage briefs it opened or bridged 3 of 12 cells unasked.
- image.motion.dolly → image.motion — "motion": "dolly" on an "image" item | does: A slow centred push-in on a held photo — the frame ends 8% larger than it starts. | needs: An image item. | cost: $0 (an ffmpeg move on her photo) | likeness risk: none | works: The fallback: a held photo with nothing in particular to arrive at, that should read as alive rather than as a slide. One thing to land on wants zoom; a wide frame wants sweep; a peak on a beat wants punch — dolly where none fits. | fails: Not a shot of her moving — that is an i2v, and it is not one. On a photo with a clear subject it wastes the arrival a zoom would make. | measured: The push-in A1b holds an own-footage i2v as; the renderer's quietest move.
- image.motion.zoom → image.motion — "motion": "zoom" on an "image" item | does: The frame closes in on a point of the photo. | needs: An image item; a focus point, or the upper-middle framing prior. | cost: $0 (an ffmpeg move on her photo) | likeness risk: none | works: A photo with one thing to arrive at — her face, a medal, the product. | fails: With no point and a busy frame it lands on the upper middle, whatever is there — a saliency point found her 0 of 8, so the prior is not a person finder. | measured: Untapped, it heads for the upper middle — within ~0.1 of her face in 8 of 8 portraits; give a focus point when the thing to arrive at sits elsewhere.
- image.motion.sweep → image.motion — "motion": "sweep" on an "image" item | does: A move across the photo's long axis at a fixed size, toward the point's side. | needs: An image item; a focus point, or it crosses from the left. | cost: $0 (an ffmpeg move on her photo) | likeness risk: none | works: A wide photo — a pitch, a line-up, a place — where the eye should travel. | fails: On a tight portrait it has nowhere to go. | measured: Same framing prior as zoom; the Board calls it Pan.
- image.motion.punch → image.motion — "motion": "punch" on an "image" item | does: A fast close-in to a point, then held — a snap on the peak. | needs: An image item; a focus point, or the framing prior. | cost: $0 (an ffmpeg move on her photo) | likeness risk: none | works: A hype edit's peak — the goal, the result — set on a beat. | fails: In a slow, reflective edit it reads as a jolt. | measured: Same framing prior as zoom; lands on a beat when the plan is on the beat.
- music.track → plan-level "music" — a track | does: One licensed track under the whole edit, cut on its beat grid when on the beat. | needs: A track from the catalogue; brand work only sees brandSafe tracks. | cost: $0 (licensed, already in the bucket) | likeness risk: none | works: Any edit; the four tracks run 84–120 BPM. | fails: No track between 90 and 114 BPM, and none above 120. | measured: Grids measured to 0.01 BPM and ≤ 6 ms; one track's second half sits half a period off.
- music.bed → plan-level "music" — a bed | does: One of six CC0 beds under the whole edit. | needs: A bed name. | cost: $0 (CC0, already in the bucket) | likeness risk: none | works: A calm or reflective edit — the beds are slow. | fails: Nothing fast enough for a hype edit. No mood tags yet — chosen by name, not feel. | measured: Five of six sit at 76–85 BPM, one at 63; the by-ear check against the grid is pending.
- look → plan-level "look" | does: One grade on every held photo — natural, warm, cool, teal-orange, muted or mono. | needs: At least one held photo on the Board. | cost: $0 (one image operation per photo) | likeness risk: none | works: An edit with held photos that should share one feel. | fails: A clip beside a graded still keeps its own colour — the two can clash. | measured: Warm and cool casts held within 6/255; clips are not graded, only stills.
  music you may name:
    track walking-around: 84 BPM, warm/reflective, energy 2 of 5
    track status: 89.99 BPM, driving/dark, energy 3 of 5
    track with-your-hands: 114.99 BPM, hype/bright, energy 4 of 5
    track save: 120 BPM, hype/driving, energy 4 of 5
    bed walking-away: 81.5 BPM, Steady and warm — a lo-fi beat that keeps moving.
    bed doodles: 85 BPM, Bright and light — easy under a fun clip.
    bed tokyo-sunset: 63 BPM, Soft and slow — for a calm, reflective cut.
    bed hope-on-repeat: 85 BPM, Hopeful and easy — a lift without the rush.
    bed we-drove-all-night: 76 BPM, Driving retro synths — the one with momentum.
    bed only-human: 85 BPM, Dark and heavy — a phonk beat for a highlight reel.
  looks you may name: natural | warm | cool | teal-orange | muted | mono"
`;
